 <NOTE N="7" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0143" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0143D"></COL> Uterque ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>manouvgrion.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk twðn touð Govtqou ceirwðn, kaiú touvtou toú mevroû ejn
wßé hßn kaqhlwmevnon toú ejrgaleiðon ejn twðé lavkkwé calavsaû,
eujqevwû ejk touð buqouð touð uådatoû toú ejrgaleiðon ajnelqoún,
eijshðlqen ejn twðé eJautouð tovpwé. 4Oper ajkanqokovpon ejrgaleiðon
ajpevdwken oJ aågioû twðé Govtqwé, eijpwvn× «1Idouú toú ejrgaleiðon, dexavmenoû touðto, ejrgavzou, kaiú mhdeún luphqhðéû</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0143"><HEAD COM="0143">CAPUT VI.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">De ferro ex profundo aquae ad manubrium reverso.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="0144B"></COL> <P COM="0144">Alio quoque tempore Gothus quidam pauper spiritu
ad conversionem venit: quem Dei vir Benedictus
 <COL N="0144C"></COL> libentissime suscepit. Quadam vero die ei dari
ferramentum jussit, quod ad falcis similitudinem <NOTE N="d" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0144" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0144D"></COL> Gemet.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod a falcis similitudine.</HI></NOTE> 
falcastrum vocatur, ut de loco quodam vepres abscinderet,
quatenus illic hortus fieri deberet. Locus
autem ipse quem <NOTE N="e" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0144" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0144D"></COL> Secundus Theod. Val.-el. et plur.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quem ad
mundandum.</HI></NOTE>  mundandum Gothus susceperat,
super ipsam laci ripam jacebat. Cumque Gothus
idem densitatem veprium totius virtutis annisu succideret,
ferrum de manubrio prosiliens in lacum cecidit,
ubi scilicet tanta erat aquarum profunditas, ut
spes requirendi ferramenti nulla jam esset. Itaque
ferro perdito, tremebundus ad Maurum monachum
cucurrit Gothus: damnum <NOTE N="f" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0144" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0144D"></COL> Id praescribitur Regulae S. P. Ben. c. 46.</NOTE>  quod fecerat nuntiavit,
et reatus sui egit poenitentiam. Quod Maurus quoque
monachus mox Benedicto famulo Dei curavit indicare.
Vir igitur Domini Benedictus haec audiens accessit
ad lacum <NOTE N="g" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0144" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0144D"></COL> Guss.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad locum.</HI></NOTE> : tulit de manu Gothi manubrium,
 <COL N="0144D"></COL> et misit in lacum: et mox ferrum de profundo rediit,
atque in manubrium intravit. Qui statim ferramentum
Gotho reddidit, dicens: Ecce labora, et noli
contristari.</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0144"><HEAD TYPE=edit COM="0144">CAPUT VII.</HEAD> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0144"><HEAD COM="0144"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>KEFAL. Z'
Periú Mauvrou monacouð touð ejpiú twðn uJdavtwn pezeuvsantoû.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="0145A"></COL> <P COM="0145"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1En miaðé twðn hJmerwðn, touð shmeiofovrou</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="1" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0145" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0145D"></COL> Uterque ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtou touð aJgivou ajndrovû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtou ajndroúû
Benedivktou ejn twðé eJautouð hJsucavzonteû kellivwé, oJ prolecqeiúû
