1En ajporivaé deú genovmenoi oiJ ajdelfoiú proúû toún touð Qeouð
aænqrwpon ajpevsteilan, ejpiú twðé aujtoún skulevnta</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="3" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0153" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0153D"></COL> Reg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>skolevnta.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpodiwðxai
 <COL N="0153B"></COL> toún ejcqroún diaú thðû eJautouð proúû Qeoún presbeivaû,
oåpwû toún livqon aørai dunhqwðsi. 4Ostiû eujqevwû paragegonwúû, kaiú eujchún poihvsaû, ejpevstreye toiðû maqhtaiðû aørai
toún livqon. Tosauvthé deú eujkovlwé spoudhðé oJ livqoû hærqh, wåste nomivzein aujtouúû mhdeún Bavroû aujtoún ejschkevnai, toú provteron
ajkivnhton oænta.</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0153"><HEAD COM="0153">CAPUT IX.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">De ingenti saxo per viri Dei orationem levato.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="0154A"></COL> <P COM="0154">Quadam die dum fratres habitacula ejusdem cellae
 <NOTE N="a" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0154" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0154D"></COL> Cellae vocabulum hic pro ipso monasterio usurpari
liquet, quod etiam in his dialogis saepissime occurrit.</NOTE>  construerent, lapis in medio jacebat quem in
aedificium levare decreverant. Cumque eum duo vel
tres movere non possent, plures adjuncti sunt, sed
ita immobilis mansit, ac si radicitus in terra teneretur:
ut palam daretur intelligi, quod super eum
ipse per se antiquus hostis sederet, quem tantorum
virorum manus movere non possent. Difficultate igitur
facta, ad virum Dei missum est ut veniret, et
orando hostem repelleret ut lapidem levare possent.
Qui mox venit, et orationem faciens benedictionem
dedit, et tanta lapis celeritate levatus est, ac si nullum
prius pondus habuisset.</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0154"><HEAD TYPE=edit COM="0154">CAPUT X.</HEAD> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0154"><HEAD COM="0154"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>KEFAL. I'.
Periú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0153" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0153D"></COL> Colb.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú touð calkouð eijdwvlou. 3Edoxen,</FOREIGN>  etc. Codex
hic in argumentis capitum semper ab editis, et a ms.
Regio discrepat.</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð euJreqevntoû calkouð zwdivou, oåqen ejxhðlqen ejn
fantasivaé toú puðr.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="0153B"></COL> <P COM="0153"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3Edoxen ouøn twðé aJgivwé toiðû oijkeivoiû ejpitrevyai maqhtaiðû,
iåna ejn twðé toúpwé ejkeivnwé, ejn wßé oJ livqoû toú priún eækeito, thún
ghðn ojruvxwsi× kataú toú prostacqeún aujtoiðû ouøn, baquú
wærugma pepoihkovteû, eiædwlon calkouðn eußron ejkeiðse, oæper
eún twðé mageireivwé rJifeún, aijfivdion puðr ejxhðlqen ajp1 aujtouð,
 <COL N="0153C"></COL> kaiú ejn ojfqalmoiðû pavntwn twðn monacwðn ejdeixe taiðû eJautouð
fantasivaiû, wJû oåti aåpan toú touð mageireivou ktivsma katekauvqh.
