deú oJ touð Qeouð aænqrwpoû touúû ajdelfouúû ejn qoruvbwé pollwðé
gegonovtaû, kaiú thún aijtivan par1 aujtwðn ejgnwkwúû, ejn twðé
mageireivwé paragevgone, kaiú toú puðr oåper eælegon oiJ ajdelfoiú
oJraðén, aujtoúû eæfaske mhdamwðû touðto qewreiðn, eujqevwû deú
thún kefalhún twðé Qewðé kataú toú sunhðqeû eijû proseuchún
klivnaû, ejdeveto uJpeúr touð ajpelqeiðn</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0153" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0153D"></COL> Reg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpelqeiðn ajpoú twðn ajdelfwðn thún ejn ojfqalmoiðû
aujtwðn fantasiwvdh cleuvh.</FOREIGN>  Colb. habet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpelaqhðnai</FOREIGN>  pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpelqeiðn.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú twðn ojfqalmwðn
twðn ajdelfwðn thún faneiðsan aujtoiðû touð ejcqrouð fantasiwvdh cleuvhn. 1Anastaúû deú ajpoú thðû proseuchðû, touúû ajpathqevntaû
twðn ajdelfwðn ojfqalmouúû ejrjrJwmevnouû
en thðé touð swvmatoû fusikhðé oJravsei ajpokatevsthse diaú thðû aujtouð proúû
toún Qeoún eJkesivaû, wåste oujkevti ejqeavsanto toú touð mageireivou ktivsma taiðû touð diabovlou flogaiðû kaiovmenon.</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0154" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0154D"></COL> Reg.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiovmenon ejn ojfqalmoiðû aujtwðn, ajll1 wJraðto loipoún
aæflekton.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajll1
ejn ojrqalmoiðû aujtwðn wJraðto aæflekton kaiú ajsavleuton.</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0153"><HEAD COM="0153">CAPUT X.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">De phantastico coquinae incendio.</HI></HEAD> <COL N="0154B"></COL> <P COM="0154">Tunc in conspectu viri Dei placuit ut in eodem
loco terram foderent. Quam dum fodiendo altius penetrarent,
aereum illic idolum fratres invenerunt.
Quo ad horam casu in coquinam projecto, exire
ignis repente visus est, atque in cunctorum monachorum
 <COL N="0154C"></COL> oculis quia omne ejusdem coquinae aedificium
consumeretur ostendit. Cumque jaciendo aquam, et
ignem quasi exstinguendo perstreperent, pulsatus
eodem tumultu vir Dei advenit. Qui eumdem ignem
in oculis fratrum esse, in suis vero non esse considerans,
caput protinus in orationem flexit, et eos quos
phantastico reperit igne deludi, revocavit fratres, ut
oculos suos signarent monuit, ut et sanum <NOTE N="b" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0154" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0154D"></COL> Gussanv., cui favent primus Theod. Gemet. et
plurimi Norm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fratres ad oculos suos, ut et sanum,</HI>  etc.</NOTE>  illud
coquinae aedificium assistere cernerent, et flammas
quas antiquus hostis finxerat, non viderent.</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0154"><HEAD TYPE=edit COM="0154">CAPUT XI.</HEAD> <DIV2 SECOND=YES COM="0154"><HEAD COM="0154"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>KEFAL. IA'.
Periú touð suntribevntoû paidoúû ejn twðé sumptwvmati.</FOREIGN></HEAD> <COL N="0155A"></COL> <P COM="0155"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Pavlin oijkodomouvntwn twðn ajdelfwðn toiðcon, kaiú eijû uåyoû
toú ktivsma aægein speudovntwn, oJ touð Qeouð qeravpwn eijû toú
eJautouð kevlion scolavzwn høn ejn thðé proseuchðé× wßétini oJ
