aægonta thún hJlikivan, uiJoún genovmenon korialivou</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="4" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> Colb.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kurialivou.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tinoúû, toú
 <COL N="0155B"></COL> gegonoúû suvmptwma sunevtriyen. OiJ deú touð aJgivou maqhtaiú
touðto eJwrakovteû kaiú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="5" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> Tria verba haec nostris mss. debentur; deerant
enim in excusis ante ed. Guss. qui ea legerat in
ms. Regio, in quo legimus et ipsi, nec non in Colb.
Alii excusi habent,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJwrakovteû ouj tosouðton.</FOREIGN></NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>perivlupoi genovmenoi, ouj tosouðton
diaú thún touð toivcou katastrofhún, oåson diaú toún touð ajdelfouð kivndunon, twðé sebasmivwé patriú Benedivktwé metaú dakruvwn
proshðlqon, toú sumbaún ajnaggevllonteû. 2O deú sumpaqevstatoû pathúr prosevtaxe touðton proúû eJautoún ejnecqhðnai, oåntina
taiðû cersiún aørai oujk iæscusan, kaq1 oåti oiJ peptwkovteû
livqoi ajpoú touð toivcou ouj movnon aujtouð toú swðma, ajllaú kaiú
taú ojstað sunevtriyan. 1Adunavtwû ouøn eæconteû taiðû cersiún,
wJû eiærhtai, touðton aørai, ajnagkaiðon hjthvsanto</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="6" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0155" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0155D"></COL> Mss.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJghvsanto,</FOREIGN> —quae vera est lectio.  <ED>EDIT</ED> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn sagivwé
